"#S4.SS3\" title=\"In 4 Methodology ‣ How Much AI Is in This Track? Quantifying the Proportion of AI-Generated Stems in Hybrid Music Mixtures\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_title\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref\">4.3 </span>Multi-track audio dataset</span></a></li>\n201\t</ol>\n202\t</li>\n203\t<li class=\"ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_section\">\n204\t<a href=\"#S5\" title=\"In How Much AI Is in This Track? Quantifying the Proportion of AI-Generated Stems in Hybrid Music Mixtures\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_title\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref\">5 </span>Experiments and Results</span></a>\n205\t<ol class=\"ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_section\">\n206\t<li class=\"ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection\"><a href=\"#S5.SS1\" title=\"In 5 Experiments and Results ‣ How Much AI Is in This Track? Quantifying the Proportion of AI-Generated Stems in Hybrid Music Mixtures\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_title\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref\">5.1 </span>Experimental Setup</span></a></li>\n207\t<li class=\"ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection\"><a href=\"#S5.SS2\" title=\"In 5 Experiments and Results ‣ How Much AI Is in This Track? Quantifying the Proportion of AI-Generated Stems in Hybrid Music Mixtures\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_title\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref\">5.2 </span>Energy-Driven Detection Response</span></a></li>\n208\t<li class=\"ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection\"><a href=\"#S5.SS3\" title=\"In 5 Experiments and Results ‣ How Much AI Is in This Track? Quantifying the Proportion of AI-Generated Stems in Hybrid Music Mixtures\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_title\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref\">5.3 </span>Instrument-Level Detection Sensitivity</span></a></li>\n209\t<li class=\"ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection\"><a href=\"#S5.SS4\" title=\"In 5 Experiments and Results ‣ How Much AI Is in This Track? Quantifying the Proportion of AI-Generated Stems in Hybrid Music Mixtures\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_title\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref\">5.4 </span>Fakeprint Analysis</span></a></li>\n210\t<li class=\"ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection\"><a href=\"#S5.SS5\" title=\"In 5 Experiments and Results ‣ How Much AI Is in This Track? Quantifying the Proportion of AI-Generated Stems in Hybrid Music Mixtures\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_title\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref\">5.5 </span>Regression Baseline</span></a></li>\n211\t</ol>\n212\t</li>\n213\t<li class=\"ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_section\"><a href=\"#S6\" title=\"In How Much AI Is in This Track? Quantifying the Proportion of AI-Generated Stems in Hybrid Music Mixtures\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_title\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref\">6 </span>Limitations</span></a></li>\n214\t<li class=\"ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_section\"><a href=\"#S7\" title=\"In How Much AI Is in This Track? Quantifying the Proportion of AI-Generated Stems in Hybrid Music Mixtures\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_title\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref\">7 </span>Conclusion</span></a></li>\n215\t<li class=\"ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_section\"><a href=\"#S8\" title=\"In How Much AI Is in This Track? Quantifying the Proportion of AI-Generated Stems in Hybrid Music Mixtures\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_title\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref\">8 </span>Acknowledgments</span></a></li>\n216\t<li class=\"ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_bibliography\"><a href=\"#bib\" title=\"In How Much AI Is in This Track? Quantifying the Proportion of AI-Generated Stems in Hybrid Music Mixtures\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_title\">References</span></a></li>\n217\t</ol></nav>\n218\t</nav>\n219\t<div class=\"ltx_page_main\">\n220\t<div id=\"infobox\" class=\"infobox\">\n221\t  <a id=\"license-tr\" href=\"https://info.arxiv.org/help/license/index.html#licenses-available\">\n222\t    License: CC BY 4.0\n223\t  </a>\n224\t  <div id=\"watermark-tr\">\n225\tarXiv:2608.07285v1 [eess.AS] 07 Aug 2026</div>\n226\t</div><div class=\"ltx_page_content\">\n227\t<article class=\"ltx_document ltx_authors_1line\">\n228\t<h1 class=\"ltx_title ltx_title_document\">How Much AI Is in This Track? Quantifying the Proportion of AI-Generated Stems in Hybrid Music Mixtures</h1>\n229\t\n230\t<div id=\"abstract1\" class=\"ltx_abstract\">\n231\t<h6 class=\"ltx_title ltx_title_abstract\">Abstract</h6>\n232\t<p class=\"ltx_p\">AI-generated music is increasingly used at the stem level, with producers integrating synthetic drums, basslines, or vocals alongside human-performed instruments. However, current AI music detection systems are binary, treating tracks as either fully AI or fully human. In this paper, we reformulate AI music detection as a regression problem on a continuous AI energy ratio, <math class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha\\in[0,1]\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha\\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. We propose a methodology that leverages a multi-track music dataset to assemble mixtures of human-performed and AI-reconstructed stems (obtained using a neural audio codec) with known proportions of each content type. Using this approach, we first show that a CNN-based model trained on fully AI-generated or human-performed tracks, which achieves <math class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"&gt;99\\%\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi></mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>99</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">&gt;99\\%</annotation></semantics></math> accuracy as a binary detector, when faced with mixed content, yields an output that rises with the AI stems’ energy contribution, acting as a noisy and miscalibrated estimator. Our analysis of the influence of different stems shows that detection sensitivity depends on the instrument and reflects its frequency content: drums and guitar carry strong codec-artifact signatures, while vocals and bass are less detectable. Based on these insights, we train a similar CNN-based model for regression of <math class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, achieving <math class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\text{MAE}=0.076\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mtext>MAE</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>0.076</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\text{MAE}=0.076</annotation></semantics></math> and <math class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"R^{2}=0.85\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.85</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R^{2}=0.85</annotation></semantics></math> on held-out mixtures from the same pipeline. These results suggest that the regression formulation is an initial promising step towards AI-music detection in realistic music production workflows.</p>\n233\t</div>\n234\t<section id=\"S1\" class=\"ltx_section\">\n235\t<h2 class=\"ltx_title ltx_title_section\">\n236\t<span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_section\">1 </span>Introduction</h2>\n237\t\n238\t<div id=\"S1.p1\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n239\t<p id=\"S1.p1.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">The prevalence of AI-generated content is growing rapidly. Industry reports estimate that fully AI-generated tracks now account for more than 50% of daily uploads on major streaming platforms <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib24\" title=\"Deezer: AI music has surpassed 50% of new music uploads for the first time\" class=\"ltx_ref\">24</a>]</cite>.\n240\tIndustry studies also report that 97% of listeners cannot reliably distinguish fully AI-generated tracks from human-made recordings <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib4\" title=\"Deezer/Ipsos survey: 97% of people can’t tell the difference between fully AI-generated and human made music – clear desire for transparency and fairness for artists\" class=\"ltx_ref\">23</a>]</cite>. This raises concerns about transparency and fair remuneration for artists and highlights the need for automated detection tools that are also aligned with disclosure obligations, such as those in Article 50 of the EU AI Act <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib17\" title=\"Technical solutions for marking and detecting AI-generated audio content in the context of article 50(2) AI act\" class=\"ltx_ref\">22</a>]</cite>.</p>\n241\t</div>\n242\t<div id=\"S1.p2\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n243\t<p id=\"S1.p2.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">Current AI music detection systems achieve near-perfect accuracy (&gt;99%) when classifying complete tracks as fully AI-generated or human-produced <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib2\" title=\"AI-generated music detection and its challenges\" class=\"ltx_ref\">2</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib7\" title=\"SONICS: synthetic or not – identifying counterfeit songs\" class=\"ltx_ref\">21</a>]</cite>. These detectors exploit architectural artifacts: the characteristic spectral peaks introduced by transposed convolution layers in neural audio codec decoders <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib1\" title=\"A Fourier explanation of AI-music artifacts\" class=\"ltx_ref\">1</a>]</cite>. Yet, it is unclear how this binary paradigm applies when AI-generated stems are combined with human performances on a single track <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib8\" title=\"Music and artificial intelligence: artistic trends\" class=\"ltx_ref\">19</a>]</cite>.</p>\n244\t</div>\n245\t<div id=\"S1.p3\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n246\t<p id=\"S1.p3.2\" class=\"ltx_p\">In this work, we reformulate AI music detection as a regression problem on a continuous AI energy ratio <math id=\"S1.p3.1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha\\in[0,1]\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha\\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, representing the proportion of a mix’s total acoustic energy contributed by AI-generated stems. Studying this reformulation requires controlled mixtures of human-performed and AI-generated stems with known <math id=\"S1.p3.2.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> values.</p>\n247\t</div>\n248\t<div id=\"S1.p4\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n249\t<p id=\"S1.p4.4\" class=\"ltx_p\">To enable this, we propose a methodology for constructing hybrid mixtures from multi-track music datasets based on three components: (i) encode–decode reconstruction of human-performed stems through a neural audio codec, which imprints the same architectural artifacts that binary detectors learn to detect while preserving the original musical content; (ii) combinatorial stem replacement, which for a track with <math id=\"S1.p4.1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"n\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math> stems produces all <math id=\"S1.p4.2.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"2^{n}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> real/AI configurations, ensuring dense sampling of <math id=\"S1.p4.3.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>; and (iii) evaluation at the level of the AI energy ratio <math id=\"S1.p4.4.m4\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, which correctly weights each stem by its acoustic contribution.</p>\n250\t</div>\n251\t<div id=\"S1.p5\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n252\t<p id=\"S1.p5.5\" class=\"ltx_p\">We apply this methodology using the MoisesDB multi-track dataset <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib5\" title=\"MoisesDB: a dataset for source separation beyond 4-stems\" class=\"ltx_ref\">17</a>]</cite> and the EnCodec neural audio codec <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib3\" title=\"High fidelity neural audio compression\" class=\"ltx_ref\">7</a>]</cite>, producing controlled mixtures across 240 professionally produced tracks. Our experiments reveal that a state-of-the-art binary detector <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib2\" title=\"AI-generated music detection and its challenges\" class=\"ltx_ref\">2</a>]</cite>, which achieves <math id=\"S1.p5.1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"&gt;99\\%\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi></mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>99</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">&gt;99\\%</annotation></semantics></math> accuracy on pure tracks, produces an output score that increases with <math id=\"S1.p5.2.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, effectively acting as a noisy and miscalibrated estimator of the AI energy ratio. Detailed analysis of the contribution of the different stems to the output indicates that the detection sensitivity is frequency-dependent: while drums and guitars are more reliably identified, vocals are only partially detected, and bass remains largely undetected. Building on these findings, we train a CNN regressor using the same architecture to estimate <math id=\"S1.p5.3.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> directly, achieving a Mean Absolute Error (MAE) of <math id=\"S1.p5.4.m4\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"0.076\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mn>0.076</mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0.076</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id=\"S1.p5.5.m5\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"R^{2}=0.85\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.85</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R^{2}=0.85</annotation></semantics></math>) on held-out mixtures from the same reconstruction pipeline.</p>\n253\t</div>\n254\t<div id=\"S1.p6\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n255\t<p id=\"S1.p6.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">The AI stems in our study are codec reconstructions of real recordings, not generator output, so what we measure is the proportion of codec-generated energy under controlled conditions (<span id=\"S1.p6.1.1\" class=\"ltx_text\">Section <a href=\"#S6\" title=\"6 Limitations ‣ How Much AI Is in This Track? Quantifying the Proportion of AI-Generated Stems in Hybrid Music Mixtures\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">6</span></a></span>). The binary detector is reproduced from Afchar et al. <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib2\" title=\"AI-generated music detection and its challenges\" class=\"ltx_ref\">2</a>]</cite> as a diagnostic probe; our contributions are the reformulation, the methodology and released library, the characterization of binary-detector behavior on hybrid mixtures, and a regression baseline.</p>\n256\t</div>\n257\t</section>\n258\t<section id=\"S2\" class=\"ltx_section\">\n259\t<h2 class=\"ltx_title ltx_title_section\">\n260\t<span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_section\">2 </span>Related Work</h2>\n261\t\n262\t<div id=\"S2.p1\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n263\t<p id=\"S2.p1.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">Neural audio codecs <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib3\" title=\"High fidelity neural audio compression\" class=\"ltx_ref\">7</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib10\" title=\"High-fidelity audio compression with improved RVQGAN\" class=\"ltx_ref\">10</a>]</cite> enable high-fidelity audio compression into discrete token sequences, and audio and music generation systems <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib14\" title=\"AudioLM: a language modeling approach to audio generation\" class=\"ltx_ref\">3</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib13\" title=\"Simple and controllable music generation\" class=\"ltx_ref\">4</a>]</cite> leverage these representations to generate music autoregressively from text or audio prompts. Other systems generate in the continuous latent space of an audio autoencoder. Stable Audio <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib18\" title=\"Fast timing-conditioned latent audio diffusion\" class=\"ltx_ref\">9</a>]</cite> synthesizes full tracks from text with latent diffusion, and Diff-A-Riff <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib19\" title=\"Diff-A-Riff: musical accompaniment co-creation via latent diffusion models\" class=\"ltx_ref\">13</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib20\" title=\"Improving musical accompaniment co-creation via diffusion transformers\" class=\"ltx_ref\">14</a>]</cite> uses the same paradigm to generate one instrument stem at a time, conditioned on a reference mix through audio or text embeddings, while LiveBand <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib21\" title=\"LiveBand: live accompaniment generation in the audio domain\" class=\"ltx_ref\">16</a>]</cite> generates accompaniment causally with an adversarially trained transformer. The latter two produce hybrid tracks directly. Whatever the conditioning, all of these systems synthesize the waveform through a learned decoder built from transposed convolution layers. These layers introduce periodic spectral artifacts <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib23\" title=\"Deconvolution and checkerboard artifacts\" class=\"ltx_ref\">15</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib22\" title=\"Upsampling artifacts in neural audio synthesis\" class=\"ltx_ref\">18</a>]</cite>, and current AI-music detectors learn to exploit them <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib1\" title=\"A Fourier explanation of AI-music artifacts\" class=\"ltx_ref\">1</a>]</cite>.</p>\n264\t</div>\n265\t<div id=\"S2.p2\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n266\t<p id=\"S2.p2.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">Early work on AI music detection focused on binary classification of complete tracks. Afchar et al. <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib2\" title=\"AI-generated music detection and its challenges\" class=\"ltx_ref\">2</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib1\" title=\"A Fourier explanation of AI-music artifacts\" class=\"ltx_ref\">1</a>]</cite> proposed a CNN-based detector that reaches 99.8% accuracy on controlled datasets by exploiting codec-induced spectral artifacts. Rahman et al. <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib7\" title=\"SONICS: synthetic or not – identifying counterfeit songs\" class=\"ltx_ref\">21</a>]</cite> proposed <span id=\"S2.p2.1.1\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_italic\">SpecTTTra</span>, a transformer with spectro-temporal tokenization that reaches an F1 score of 97% on full-track detection. However, these detectors face important limitations. Generalization difficulties across generators were already noted by Afchar et al., and Cros Vila et al. <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib9\" title=\"The AI music arms race: on the detection of AI-generated music\" class=\"ltx_ref\">5</a>]</cite> further demonstrated that binary detectors exhibit strong platform-specific biases: a detector trained on music from one generation platform fails to generalize to another. What these detectors learn is therefore specific to a generator, not a universal signature of AI-generated audio. Afchar et al. <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib2\" title=\"AI-generated music detection and its challenges\" class=\"ltx_ref\">2</a>]</cite> also showed that simple audio transformations, such as pitch shifting or re-encoding, significantly degrade detection accuracy, exposing vulnerability to post-processing. Detection also degrades on broadcast audio, where music is often short and mixed with speech; F1 scores fall below 60% <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib16\" title=\"AI-generated music detection in broadcast monitoring\" class=\"ltx_ref\">11</a>]</cite>.</p>\n267\t</div>\n268\t<div id=\"S2.p3\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n269\t<p id=\"S2.p3.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">A similar redefinition of the detection of AI-generated content has already taken place in adjacent fields. In visual deepfake detection, recent work reformulates the task as multi-label classification over individual facial components or predicts pixel-level masks that localize manipulated regions within video frames <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib15\" title=\"A multi-label classification method based on transformer for deepfake detection\" class=\"ltx_ref\">8</a>, <a href=\"#bib.bib25\" title=\"Localization and detection of deepfake videos based on self-blending method\" class=\"ltx_ref\">25</a>]</cite>.</p>\n270\t</div>\n271\t<div id=\"S2.p4\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n272\t<p id=\"S2.p4.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">While existing detectors achieve high accuracy (&gt;99%) on binary classification of fully AI-generated tracks, to our knowledge no prior work has examined detection when AI-generated content is mixed with human-created content at varying proportions. This setting is increasingly relevant as professional production integrates AI-generated components with human performances <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib8\" title=\"Music and artificial intelligence: artistic trends\" class=\"ltx_ref\">19</a>]</cite>, a practice that the stem- and accompaniment-generation models discussed above directly support. Yet detectors trained under the assumption of either fully AI or fully human music can exhibit degraded performance on mixed content (<span id=\"S2.p4.1.1\" class=\"ltx_text\">Section <a href=\"#S5\" title=\"5 Experiments and Results ‣ How Much AI Is in This Track? Quantifying the Proportion of AI-Generated Stems in Hybrid Music Mixtures\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">5</span></a></span>). Motivated by this gap, and supported by the shift toward partial detection in adjacent fields, we study proportional AI content detection at the stem level and propose a regression baseline for the task.</p>\n273\t</div>\n274\t</section>\n275\t<section id=\"S3\" class=\"ltx_section\">\n276\t<h2 class=\"ltx_title ltx_title_section\">\n277\t<span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_section\">3 </span>Problem Formulation</h2>\n278\t\n279\t<section id=\"S3.SS1\" class=\"ltx_subsection\">\n280\t<h3 class=\"ltx_title ltx_title_subsection\">\n281\t<span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection\">3.1 </span>Binary AI-music Detection</h3>\n282\t\n283\t<div id=\"S3.SS1.p1\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n284\t<p id=\"S3.SS1.p1.6\" class=\"ltx_p\">In prior work, AI music detection has been formulated as a binary classification problem <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib2\" title=\"AI-generated music detection and its challenges\" class=\"ltx_ref\">2</a>]</cite>.\n285\tGiven an audio signal <math id=\"S3.SS1.p1.1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\mathbf{x}\\in\\mathbf{R}^{T\\times C}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>𝐑</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace=\"0.222em\" rspace=\"0.222em\">×</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbf{x}\\in\\mathbf{R}^{T\\times C}</annotation></semantics></math> (where <math id=\"S3.SS1.p1.2.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"T\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of samples\n286\tand <math id=\"S3.SS1.p1.3.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"C\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of channels), the task is to predict <math id=\"S3.SS1.p1.4.m4\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"y\\in\\{0,1\\}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y\\in\\{0,1\\}</annotation></semantics></math>,\n287\twhere <math id=\"S3.SS1.p1.5.m5\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"y=0\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y=0</annotation></semantics></math> indicates human-produced music and <math id=\"S3.SS1.p1.6.m6\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"y=1\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y=1</annotation></semantics></math> indicates AI-generated music.</p>\n288\t</div>\n289\t<div id=\"S3.SS1.p2\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n290\t<p id=\"S3.SS1.p2.2\" class=\"ltx_p\">The detectors identify artifacts in the form of spectral peaks introduced by the transposed convolution layers of the decoder, the audio counterpart of the <span id=\"S3.SS1.p2.2.1\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_italic\">checkerboard\n291\tartifacts</span> of image generation <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib23\" title=\"Deconvolution and checkerboard artifacts\" class=\"ltx_ref\">15</a>]</cite>. Afchar et al. <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib1\" title=\"A Fourier explanation of AI-music artifacts\" class=\"ltx_ref\">1</a>]</cite> call this signature an <em id=\"S3.SS1.p2.2.2\" class=\"ltx_emph ltx_font_italic\">artifact fingerprint</em>, and in their released code, a <em id=\"S3.SS1.p2.2.3\" class=\"ltx_emph ltx_font_italic\">fakeprint</em>, the term we use here. The peaks appear at\n292\t<math id=\"S3.SS1.p2.1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"f_{\\text{artifact}}=f_{s}/(2\\times\\text{stride})\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>artifact</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace=\"0.222em\" rspace=\"0.222em\">×</mo><mtext>stride</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f_{\\text{artifact}}=f_{s}/(2\\times\\text{stride})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id=\"S3.SS1.p2.2.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"f_{s}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> is the sampling rate. Because the strides are fixed by the architecture, the peaks appear at the same frequencies in all audio the decoder generates.</p>\n293\t</div>\n294\t</section>\n295\t<section id=\"S3.SS2\" class=\"ltx_subsection\">\n296\t<h3 class=\"ltx_title ltx_title_subsection\">\n297\t<span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection\">3.2 </span>Mixed-Content Production Scenarios</h3>\n298\t\n299\t<div id=\"S3.SS2.p1\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n300\t<p id=\"S3.SS2.p1.5\" class=\"ltx_p\">Assuming a linear mixture, a track is the sum of <math id=\"S3.SS2.p1.1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"n\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math> stems, <math id=\"S3.SS2.p1.2.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"x_{\\text{mix}}=\\sum_{i=1}^{n}s_{i}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mtext>mix</mtext></msub><mo rspace=\"0.111em\">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_{\\text{mix}}=\\sum_{i=1}^{n}s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>,\n301\twhere each stem <math id=\"S3.SS2.p1.3.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"s_{i}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is either human-produced (<math id=\"S3.SS2.p1.4.m4\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"s_{i}\\in H\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s_{i}\\in H</annotation></semantics></math>) or AI-generated\n302\t(<math id=\"S3.SS2.p1.5.m5\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"s_{i}\\in A\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s_{i}\\in A</annotation></semantics></math>).\n303\tTo quantify the AI content of a mix, we define the <em id=\"S3.SS2.p1.5.1\" class=\"ltx_emph ltx_font_italic\">AI energy ratio</em></p>\n304\t</div>\n305\t<div id=\"S3.SS2.p2\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n306\t<table id=\"S3.E1\" class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table\">\n307\t\n308\t<tbody><tr class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline\">\n309\t<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft\"></td>\n310\t<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center\"><math id=\"S3.E1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha=\\frac{\\sum_{s_{i}\\in A}\\mathrm{RMS}(s_{i})^{2}}{\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\mathrm{RMS}(s_{i})^{2}},\" display=\"block\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>RMS</mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>RMS</mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha=\\frac{\\sum_{s_{i}\\in A}\\mathrm{RMS}(s_{i})^{2}}{\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\mathrm{RMS}(s_{i})^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n311\t<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright\"></td>\n312\t<td rowspan=\"1\" class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right\">(1)</span></td>\n313\t</tr></tbody>\n314\t</table>\n315\t</div>\n316\t<div id=\"S3.SS2.p3\" class=\"ltx_para ltx_noindent\">\n317\t<p id=\"S3.SS2.p3.2\" class=\"ltx_p\">where <math id=\"S3.SS2.p3.1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\mathrm{RMS}(\\cdot)\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>RMS</mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">⋅</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{RMS}(\\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the root-mean-square waveform amplitude values of a stem and <math id=\"S3.SS2.p3.2.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>\n318\tis the fraction of total signal energy contributed by AI-generated stems.</p>\n319\t</div>\n320\t<div id=\"S3.SS2.p4\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n321\t<p id=\"S3.SS2.p4.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">Mixing alters artifact detectability. The spectral peaks are present only in the AI stems, so combining them with human content in overlapping frequency bands reduces their prominence relative to the surrounding spectrum.</p>\n322\t</div>\n323\t</section>\n324\t<section id=\"S3.SS3\" class=\"ltx_subsection\">\n325\t<h3 class=\"ltx_title ltx_title_subsection\">\n326\t<span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection\">3.3 </span>Proportional Detection via Regression</h3>\n327\t\n328\t<div id=\"S3.SS3.p1\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n329\t<p id=\"S3.SS3.p1.5\" class=\"ltx_p\">We reformulate AI music detection as a regression problem. Given a\n330\tmixed audio signal <math id=\"S3.SS3.p1.1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"x_{\\text{mix}}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mtext>mix</mtext></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_{\\text{mix}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the task is to predict\n331\t<math id=\"S3.SS3.p1.2.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\hat{\\alpha}=f_{\\theta}(x_{\\text{mix}})\\in[0,1]\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>α</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mtext>mix</mtext></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\hat{\\alpha}=f_{\\theta}(x_{\\text{mix}})\\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id=\"S3.SS3.p1.3.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\hat{\\alpha}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>α</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\hat{\\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>\n332\tis the estimated AI energy ratio and <math id=\"S3.SS3.p1.4.m4\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"f_{\\theta}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f_{\\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is a learned function\n333\tparameterized by <math id=\"S3.SS3.p1.5.m5\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\theta\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\theta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>\n334\t</div>\n335\t<div id=\"S3.SS3.p2\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n336\t<p id=\"S3.SS3.p2.4\" class=\"ltx_p\">We report mean absolute error (MAE) and root mean squared error (RMSE) in the\n337\tunits of <math id=\"S3.SS3.p2.1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, the coefficient of determination (<math id=\"S3.SS3.p2.2.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"R^{2}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>), and Pearson’s <math id=\"S3.SS3.p2.3.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"r\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r</annotation></semantics></math>. A proportional output such as\n338\t“approximately <math id=\"S3.SS3.p2.4.m4\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"X\\%\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X\\%</annotation></semantics></math> AI-generated” carries more information than a binary label and better\n339\treflects hybrid production workflows.</p>\n340\t</div>\n341\t</section>\n342\t<section id=\"S3.SS4\" class=\"ltx_subsection\">\n343\t<h3 class=\"ltx_title ltx_title_subsection\">\n344\t<span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection\">3.4 </span>Key Challenges</h3>\n345\t\n346\t<div id=\"S3.SS4.p1\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n347\t<p id=\"S3.SS4.p1.2\" class=\"ltx_p\">This reformulation introduces two challenges beyond binary classification. Regression must\n348\tdistinguish arbitrary values of <math id=\"S3.SS4.p1.1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, and the same <math id=\"S3.SS4.p1.2.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> can arise from different stem\n349\tcombinations (50% AI vocals versus 50% AI drums), so detectability depends on <em id=\"S3.SS4.p1.2.1\" class=\"ltx_emph ltx_font_italic\">how much</em>\n350\tenergy the AI stems contribute and on <em id=\"S3.SS4.p1.2.2\" class=\"ltx_emph ltx_font_italic\">where</em> in the spectrum that energy lies.</p>\n351\t</div>\n352\t</section>\n353\t</section>\n354\t<section id=\"S4\" class=\"ltx_section\">\n355\t<h2 class=\"ltx_title ltx_title_section\">\n356\t<span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_section\">4 </span>Methodology</h2>\n357\t\n358\t<div id=\"S4.p1\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n359\t<p id=\"S4.p1.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">We introduce a methodology for constructing controlled hybrid mixtures of\n360\thuman-performed and AI-generated stems with a known AI energy ratio\n361\t<math id=\"S4.p1.1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, as defined in <span id=\"S4.p1.1.1\" class=\"ltx_text\">Eqn (<a href=\"#S3.E1\" title=\"In 3.2 Mixed-Content Production Scenarios ‣ 3 Problem Formulation ‣ How Much AI Is in This Track? Quantifying the Proportion of AI-Generated Stems in Hybrid Music Mixtures\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">1</span></a>)</span>. Note that the AI-generated stems in our study are codec reconstructions of real recordings.</p>\n362\t</div>\n363\t<div id=\"S4.p2\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n364\t<p id=\"S4.p2.2\" class=\"ltx_p\">The methodology is guided by three principles:\n365\t(1) <em id=\"S4.p2.2.1\" class=\"ltx_emph ltx_font_italic\">stem-level granularity</em>, reflecting the modular structure of modern\n366\tproduction; (2) <em id=\"S4.p2.2.2\" class=\"ltx_emph ltx_font_italic\">artifact isolation through reconstruction</em>, which reduces\n367\tcontent confounds between AI and human conditions; and (3)\n368\t<em id=\"S4.p2.2.3\" class=\"ltx_emph ltx_font_italic\">combinatorial completeness</em>, which provides dense coverage of <math id=\"S4.p2.1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>\n369\tover the full <math id=\"S4.p2.2.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"[0,1]\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> range. The methodology is agnostic to both the source corpus\n370\t(any multi-track dataset with isolated stems can serve as input)\n371\tand the codec used for reconstruction.</p>\n372\t</div>\n373\t<section id=\"S4.SS1\" class=\"ltx_subsection\">\n374\t<h3 class=\"ltx_title ltx_title_subsection\">\n375\t<span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection\">4.1 </span>AI Reconstruction Pipeline</h3>\n376\t\n377\t<div id=\"S4.SS1.p1\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n378\t<p id=\"S4.SS1.p1.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">We build AI stems by encoding and decoding existing human-performed stems\n379\tthrough a neural audio codec. This encode–decode process introduces the characteristic spectral\n380\tartifacts of the decoder’s transposed convolution layers <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib1\" title=\"A Fourier explanation of AI-music artifacts\" class=\"ltx_ref\">1</a>]</cite>\n381\twhile preserving the original musical content. This isolates the detection problem to\n382\tarchitectural artifacts, eliminating confounds from differences in musical style or\n383\tcontent between the AI and human conditions. The process is deterministic and therefore reproducible.\n384\tThe methodology is also codec-agnostic; any neural codec exposing encode and decode operations can be substituted.</p>\n385\t</div>\n386\t<div id=\"S4.SS1.p2\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n387\t<p id=\"S4.SS1.p2.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">We instantiate the pipeline with EnCodec <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib3\" title=\"High fidelity neural audio compression\" class=\"ltx_ref\">7</a>]</cite>,\n388\treconstructing stems at a single bitrate of 3 kbps.\n389\tWhen reproducing the evaluation conditions in <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib2\" title=\"AI-generated music detection and its challenges\" class=\"ltx_ref\">2</a>]</cite>, the reconstructed stems are stored as MP3 at 256 kbps, 44.1 kHz, so that any observed detection failure on mixed content is attributable to the mixing process and not to a format mismatch.</p>\n390\t</div>\n391\t</section>\n392\t<section id=\"S4.SS2\" class=\"ltx_subsection\">\n393\t<h3 class=\"ltx_title ltx_title_subsection\">\n394\t<span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection\">4.2 </span>Combinatorial Mix Generation</h3>\n395\t\n396\t<div id=\"S4.SS2.p1\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n397\t<p id=\"S4.SS2.p1.3\" class=\"ltx_p\">Given a track with <math id=\"S4.SS2.p1.1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"n\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math> stems indexed by <math id=\"S4.SS2.p1.2.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"I=\\{0,1,\\ldots,n-1\\}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I=\\{0,1,\\ldots,n-1\\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we\n398\tdefine a mix specification by the subset <math id=\"S4.SS2.p1.3.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"S\\subseteq I\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S\\subseteq I</annotation></semantics></math> of stems replaced\n399\twith their AI-reconstructed versions. The resulting mix is</p>\n400\t<table id=\"S4.E2\" class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table\">\n401\t\n402\t<tbody><tr class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline\">\n403\t<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft\"></td>\n404\t<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center\"><math id=\"S4.E2.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"x_{\\text{mix}}(S)=\\sum_{i\\in I\\setminus S}s_{i}^{\\text{real}}+\\sum_{i\\in S}s_{i}^{\\text{AI}},\" display=\"block\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mtext>mix</mtext></msub><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace=\"0.111em\">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits=\"false\">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>real</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace=\"0.055em\">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits=\"false\">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>AI</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_{\\text{mix}}(S)=\\sum_{i\\in I\\setminus S}s_{i}^{\\text{real}}+\\sum_{i\\in S}s_{i}^{\\text{AI}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n405\t<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright\"></td>\n406\t<td rowspan=\"1\" class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right\">(2)</span></td>\n407\t</tr></tbody>\n408\t</table>\n409\t<p id=\"S4.SS2.p1.6\" class=\"ltx_p\">where <math id=\"S4.SS2.p1.4.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"s_{i}^{\\text{real}}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>real</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s_{i}^{\\text{real}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id=\"S4.SS2.p1.5.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"s_{i}^{\\text{AI}}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>AI</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">s_{i}^{\\text{AI}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the authentic and\n410\tAI-reconstructed versions of stem <math id=\"S4.SS2.p1.6.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"i\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Stems are summed with equal weights,\n411\tpreserving the original energy relationships defined by the source mix.</p>\n412\t</div>\n413\t<div id=\"S4.SS2.p2\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n414\t<p id=\"S4.SS2.p2.6\" class=\"ltx_p\">We organize mixes into sets indexed by the number of AI-reconstructed stems:</p>\n415\t<table id=\"S4.E3\" class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table\">\n416\t\n417\t<tbody><tr class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline\">\n418\t<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft\"></td>\n419\t<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center\"><math id=\"S4.E3.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"U_{k}=\\left\\{x_{\\text{mix}}(S):S\\subseteq I,\\;|S|=k\\right\\},\\quad k=0,1,\\ldots,n.\" display=\"block\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mtext>mix</mtext></msub><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo rspace=\"0.278em\" stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace=\"0.278em\">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo rspace=\"0.447em\">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace=\"1.167em\">,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U_{k}=\\left\\{x_{\\text{mix}}(S):S\\subseteq I,\\;|S|=k\\right\\},\\quad k=0,1,\\ldots,n.</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n420\t<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright\"></td>\n421\t<td rowspan=\"1\" class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right\">(3)</span></td>\n422\t</tr></tbody>\n423\t</table>\n424\t<p id=\"S4.SS2.p2.5\" class=\"ltx_p\">Each set <math id=\"S4.SS2.p2.1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"U_{k}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> contains <math id=\"S4.SS2.p2.2.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\binom{n}{k}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"0pt\"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\binom{n}{k}</annotation></semantics></math> mixes, for a total of <math id=\"S4.SS2.p2.3.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"2^{n}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> mixes\n425\tper track. The ratio <math id=\"S4.SS2.p2.4.m4\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"k/n\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k/n</annotation></semantics></math>, the <em id=\"S4.SS2.p2.5.1\" class=\"ltx_emph ltx_font_italic\">stem fraction</em>, counts <em id=\"S4.SS2.p2.5.2\" class=\"ltx_emph ltx_font_italic\">how many</em> stems are replaced, whereas the target variable <math id=\"S4.SS2.p2.5.m5\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> (<span id=\"S4.SS2.p2.5.3\" class=\"ltx_text\">Eqn (<a href=\"#S3.E1\" title=\"In 3.2 Mixed-Content Production Scenarios ‣ 3 Problem Formulation ‣ How Much AI Is in This Track? Quantifying the Proportion of AI-Generated Stems in Hybrid Music Mixtures\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">1</span></a>)</span>) weights each stem by its energy.</p>\n426\t</div>\n427\t<div id=\"S4.SS2.p3\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n428\t<p id=\"S4.SS2.p3.5\" class=\"ltx_p\">Sets <math id=\"S4.SS2.p3.1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"U_{0}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (all real) and <math id=\"S4.SS2.p3.2.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"U_{n}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> (all AI) correspond to the binary detection setting; the\n429\tintermediate sets <math id=\"S4.SS2.p3.3.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"U_{1},\\ldots,U_{n-1}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U_{1},\\ldots,U_{n-1}</annotation></semantics></math> contain the mixed-content cases. Within a set, mixes\n430\tshare the stem fraction <math id=\"S4.SS2.p3.4.m4\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"k/n\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k/n</annotation></semantics></math> but span a range of <math id=\"S4.SS2.p3.5.m5\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> values and differ in which instruments\n431\tare AI. This last property is what enables the instrument-level analysis of\n432\t<span id=\"S4.SS2.p3.5.1\" class=\"ltx_text\">Section <a href=\"#S5.SS3\" title=\"5.3 Instrument-Level Detection Sensitivity ‣ 5 Experiments and Results ‣ How Much AI Is in This Track? Quantifying the Proportion of AI-Generated Stems in Hybrid Music Mixtures\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">5.3</span></a></span>.</p>\n433\t</div>\n434\t</section>\n435\t<section id=\"S4.SS3\" class=\"ltx_subsection\">\n436\t<h3 class=\"ltx_title ltx_title_subsection\">\n437\t<span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection\">4.3 </span>Multi-track audio dataset</h3>\n438\t\n439\t<div id=\"S4.SS3.p1\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n440\t<p id=\"S4.SS3.p1.3\" class=\"ltx_p\">The methodology applies to any multi-track dataset providing isolated stems,\n441\tincluding those developed for source separation (e.g., MUSDB18 <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib12\" title=\"The MUSDB18 corpus for music separation\" class=\"ltx_ref\">20</a>]</cite>, Slakh <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib11\" title=\"Cutting music source separation some Slakh: a dataset to study the impact of training data quality and quantity\" class=\"ltx_ref\">12</a>]</cite>).\n442\tWe instantiate the methodology on MoisesDB <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib5\" title=\"MoisesDB: a dataset for source separation beyond 4-stems\" class=\"ltx_ref\">17</a>]</cite>, a professionally\n443\tmixed multi-track dataset providing high-quality stem isolations across\n444\tdiverse genres. We use 240 tracks, with stem counts ranging from 2 to 10 (most tracks contain 4–7 stems)\n445\tcategorized by instrument type (vocals, drums, bass, guitar, and other\n446\tinstruments such as keyboards, strings, and synthesizers). The variable stem count is a feature of the design: tracks with different <math id=\"S4.SS3.p1.1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"n\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math> produce different sets of\n447\tachievable <math id=\"S4.SS3.p1.2.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> values, and aggregated across the corpus, these provide dense\n448\tcoverage of the full <math id=\"S4.SS3.p1.3.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"[0,1]\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> range, with most mixes concentrated around mid-range values. In total, this yields 21,212 unique mixes across the 240 tracks.</p>\n449\t</div>\n450\t<div id=\"S4.SS3.p2\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n451\t<p id=\"S4.SS3.p2.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">We release a reproducible Python library<span id=\"footnote1\" class=\"ltx_note ltx_role_footnote\"><sup class=\"ltx_note_mark\">1</sup><span class=\"ltx_note_outer\"><span class=\"ltx_note_content\"><sup class=\"ltx_note_mark\">1</sup><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_note\">1</span>ARIA (Authentic vs. Reconstructed Isolated Audio); code available at <a href=\"https://github.com/fergarciadlc/aria\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter\">https://github.com/fergarciadlc/aria</a>.</span></span></span> that constructs mixtures from a local MoisesDB installation.</p>\n452\t</div>\n453\t</section>\n454\t</section>\n455\t<section id=\"S5\" class=\"ltx_section\">\n456\t<h2 class=\"ltx_title ltx_title_section\">\n457\t<span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_section\">5 </span>Experiments and Results</h2>\n458\t\n459\t<div id=\"S5.p1\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n460\t<p id=\"S5.p1.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">We apply the methodology of <span id=\"S5.p1.1.1\" class=\"ltx_text\">Section <a href=\"#S4\" title=\"4 Methodology ‣ How Much AI Is in This Track? Quantifying the Proportion of AI-Generated Stems in Hybrid Music Mixtures\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">4</span></a></span> to construct hybrid mixtures and compare two models on them: the reproduced binary detector, and a regression model with the same backbone trained on <math id=\"S5.p1.1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>\n461\t</div>\n462\t<section id=\"S5.SS1\" class=\"ltx_subsection\">\n463\t<h3 class=\"ltx_title ltx_title_subsection\">\n464\t<span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection\">5.1 </span>Experimental Setup</h3>\n465\t\n466\t<div id=\"S5.SS1.p1\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n467\t<p id=\"S5.SS1.p1.3\" class=\"ltx_p\"><span id=\"S5.SS1.p1.3.1\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_bold\">Models</span>. Following <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib2\" title=\"AI-generated music detection and its challenges\" class=\"ltx_ref\">2</a>]</cite>, we implement a CNN classifier: a six-block convolutional backbone operating on magnitude spectrograms (STFT with 2048-sample window, 512-sample hop, frequencies above 16 kHz discarded), followed by global average pooling and a dense head. We train two variants of this architecture that differ only in their output layer and loss. The binary detector uses a sigmoid-activated classification head trained with binary cross-entropy on the original <math id=\"S5.SS1.p1.1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\{0,1\\}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\{0,1\\}</annotation></semantics></math> labels.\n468\tThe regression model replaces the classification head with a single-unit, sigmoid-activated regression head trained with mean squared error against the AI energy ratio <math id=\"S5.SS1.p1.2.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> (<span id=\"S5.SS1.p1.3.2\" class=\"ltx_text\">Eqn (<a href=\"#S3.E1\" title=\"In 3.2 Mixed-Content Production Scenarios ‣ 3 Problem Formulation ‣ How Much AI Is in This Track? Quantifying the Proportion of AI-Generated Stems in Hybrid Music Mixtures\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">1</span></a>)</span>).\n469\tAt inference, both models produce per-window scores <math id=\"S5.SS1.p1.3.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\hat{y}\\in[0,1]\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\hat{y}\\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, which are averaged across non-overlapping windows to obtain a track-level score.</p>\n470\t</div>\n471\t<div id=\"S5.SS1.p2\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n472\t<p id=\"S5.SS1.p2.1\" class=\"ltx_p\"><span id=\"S5.SS1.p2.1.1\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_bold\">Training.</span> The binary detector is trained on FMA-Medium <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib6\" title=\"FMA: a dataset for music analysis\" class=\"ltx_ref\">6</a>]</cite> and its EnCodec-reconstructed counterpart at 3 kbps, following the original methodology by Afchar et al. <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib2\" title=\"AI-generated music detection and its challenges\" class=\"ltx_ref\">2</a>]</cite>. The regression model is trained on the hybrid mixtures produced by our methodology applied to MoisesDB at the 3 kbps EnCodec condition (<span id=\"S5.SS1.p2.1.2\" class=\"ltx_text\">Section <a href=\"#S4.SS3\" title=\"4.3 Multi-track audio dataset ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ How Much AI Is in This Track? Quantifying the Proportion of AI-Generated Stems in Hybrid Music Mixtures\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">4.3</span></a></span>), with <math id=\"S5.SS1.p2.1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> computed per 5-second window as the regression target.</p>\n473\t</div>\n474\t<div id=\"S5.SS1.p3\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n475\t<p id=\"S5.SS1.p3.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">We initially trained both models on 1-second windows, matching prior work <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib2\" title=\"AI-generated music detection and its challenges\" class=\"ltx_ref\">2</a>]</cite>. The regression model performed better with 5-second windows, particularly near the boundaries of the <math id=\"S5.SS1.p3.1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> range where short windows produced noisier estimates, so we retrained the binary detector at 5-second windows as well and report the matched comparison throughout. <span id=\"S5.SS1.p3.1.1\" class=\"ltx_text\">Section <a href=\"#S5.SS5\" title=\"5.5 Regression Baseline ‣ 5 Experiments and Results ‣ How Much AI Is in This Track? Quantifying the Proportion of AI-Generated Stems in Hybrid Music Mixtures\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">5.5</span></a></span> reports both window lengths.\n476\tTrain, validation, and test splits are performed at the track level, stratified by stem count, so that all mixes and all windows from a given track land in the same partition, preventing content and temporal-correlation leakage. The 240 tracks are split 80/10/10, leaving 24 held-out tracks and 1,792 test mixtures.</p>\n477\t</div>\n478\t<div id=\"S5.SS1.p4\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n479\t<p id=\"S5.SS1.p4.2\" class=\"ltx_p\"><span id=\"S5.SS1.p4.2.1\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_bold\">Reproduction validation.</span> The binary detector achieves 99.97% accuracy and 99.98% F1 on a held-out FMA evaluation set, closely matching <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib2\" title=\"AI-generated music detection and its challenges\" class=\"ltx_ref\">2</a>]</cite>. On the pure endpoints <math id=\"S5.SS1.p4.1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"U_{0}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id=\"S5.SS1.p4.2.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"U_{n}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> of our mixture corpus, the detector assigns scores near 0 and 1, respectively, confirming that the reconstruction pipeline preserves the codec artifacts on which the binary classifier relies.</p>\n480\t</div>\n481\t<div id=\"S5.SS1.p5\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n482\t<p id=\"S5.SS1.p5.1\" class=\"ltx_p\"><span id=\"S5.SS1.p5.1.1\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_bold\">Evaluation.</span> We run inference on the held-out test split and report track-level scores, obtained by averaging the per-window scores of each mixture; the instrument-level analysis of <span id=\"S5.SS1.p5.1.2\" class=\"ltx_text\">Section <a href=\"#S5.SS3\" title=\"5.3 Instrument-Level Detection Sensitivity ‣ 5 Experiments and Results ‣ How Much AI Is in This Track? Quantifying the Proportion of AI-Generated Stems in Hybrid Music Mixtures\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">5.3</span></a></span> uses window scores directly.</p>\n483\t</div>\n484\t</section>\n485\t<section id=\"S5.SS2\" class=\"ltx_subsection\">\n486\t<h3 class=\"ltx_title ltx_title_subsection\">\n487\t<span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection\">5.2 </span>Energy-Driven Detection Response</h3>\n488\t\n489\t<div id=\"S5.SS2.p1\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n490\t<p id=\"S5.SS2.p1.2\" class=\"ltx_p\">We first examine how each model’s output <math id=\"S5.SS2.p1.1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\hat{y}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\hat{y}</annotation></semantics></math> depends on the AI energy ratio <math id=\"S5.SS2.p1.2.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> (Figure <a href=\"#S5.F1\" title=\"Figure 1 ‣ 5.2 Energy-Driven Detection Response ‣ 5 Experiments and Results ‣ How Much AI Is in This Track? Quantifying the Proportion of AI-Generated Stems in Hybrid Music Mixtures\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">1</span></a>, medians binned in 10% increments, both models at 5-second windows).</p>\n491\t</div>\n492\t<div id=\"S5.SS2.p2\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n493\t<p id=\"S5.SS2.p2.7\" class=\"ltx_p\">The binary detector’s output increases with <math id=\"S5.SS2.p2.1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, but the increase is not linear: its median stays near <math id=\"S5.SS2.p2.2.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"0.05\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mn>0.05</mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0.05</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id=\"S5.SS2.p2.3.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha&lt;0.5\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha&lt;0.5</annotation></semantics></math> and then rises to <math id=\"S5.SS2.p2.4.m4\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\sim 0.97\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi></mi><mo>∼</mo><mn>0.97</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sim 0.97</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id=\"S5.SS2.p2.5.m5\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha&gt;0.9\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha&gt;0.9</annotation></semantics></math>. The detector was trained only on the endpoints <math id=\"S5.SS2.p2.6.m6\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha\\in\\{0,1\\}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha\\in\\{0,1\\}</annotation></semantics></math> and has never seen mixed content, so this response shows that codec artifacts in hybrid mixtures carry proportional information about AI content, which the binary classifier picks up incidentally as a noisy and miscalibrated estimator of <math id=\"S5.SS2.p2.7.m7\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>\n494\t</div>\n495\t<div id=\"S5.SS2.p3\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n496\t<p id=\"S5.SS2.p3.4\" class=\"ltx_p\">The regression model, trained directly on <math id=\"S5.SS2.p3.1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, follows the diagonal across the full range, while the binary detector underestimates AI content in the low and mid range: at <math id=\"S5.SS2.p3.2.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha\\in[0.4,0.5]\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>0.4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha\\in[0.4,0.5]</annotation></semantics></math> its median is <math id=\"S5.SS2.p3.3.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"0.10\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mn>0.10</mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0.10</annotation></semantics></math>, against <math id=\"S5.SS2.p3.4.m4\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"0.44\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mn>0.44</mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0.44</annotation></semantics></math> for the regression model. Part of this gap comes from window length (<span id=\"S5.SS2.p3.4.1\" class=\"ltx_text\">Section <a href=\"#S5.SS5\" title=\"5.5 Regression Baseline ‣ 5 Experiments and Results ‣ How Much AI Is in This Track? Quantifying the Proportion of AI-Generated Stems in Hybrid Music Mixtures\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">5.5</span></a></span>). The proportional signal is therefore present in mixed content, and the training objective determines how well it is recovered.</p>\n497\t</div>\n498\t<figure id=\"S5.F1\" class=\"ltx_figure\"><img src=\"2608.07285v1/x1.png\" id=\"S5.F1.g1\" class=\"ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape\" width=\"830\" height=\"519\" alt=\"Refer to caption\">\n499\t<figcaption class=\"ltx_caption ltx_centering\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure\"><span id=\"S5.F1.6.1.1\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_bold\">Figure 1</span>: </span>Median <math id=\"S5.F1.3.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\hat{y}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\hat{y}</annotation></semantics></math> as a function\n500\tof the AI energy ratio <math id=\"S5.F1.4.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> for the binary and regression models, both at 5-second windows; error bars show the interquartile range.</figcaption>\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "d6f576ca-1307-49f4-8bfb-38cd36c1c90f", "uuid": "a328a3c9-3a0b-4c53-9902-07bb555a2fb7", "timestamp": "2026-08-10T06:45:23.692Z", "tool_use_result": {"type": "text", "file": {"filePath": "/tmp/paper_2608.07285v1.html", "content": "<!DOCTYPE html><html prefix=\"dcterms: http://purl.org/dc/terms/\" lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta http-equiv=\"content-type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\">\n<title>How Much AI Is in This Track? Quantifying the Proportion of AI-Generated Stems in Hybrid Music Mixtures</title>\n<!--Generated on Fri Aug  7 14:24:39 2026 by LaTeXML (version 0.8.8) http://dlmf.nist.gov/LaTeXML/.-->\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, shrink-to-fit=no\">\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/static/browse/0.3.4/css/arxiv-html-papers-20260131.css\" type=\"text/css\">\n<script src=\"/static/browse/0.3.4/js/arxiv-html-papers-20260131.js\"></script>\n<script>\n  // Restore the saved color scheme preference, or\n  // enact the browser preference if \"automatic\", \n  // without expecting DOM load to have completed.\n  //\n  // Also restore any saved readingmode and ToC display preferences.\n  function initializeReadingPreferences() {\n    let saved_theme = localStorage.getItem(\"ar5iv_theme\") || \"automatic\";\n    if (saved_theme === \"automatic\") {\n      if (window.matchMedia(\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\").matches) {\n        saved_theme = \"dark\";\n      }\n    }\n    if (saved_theme == \"dark\") {\n      document.documentElement.setAttribute(\"data-theme\", \"dark\");\n    } else {\n      document.documentElement.setAttribute(\"data-theme\", \"light\");\n    }\n\n    const tocDisplay = localStorage.getItem('arxiv_html_paper_toc_display');\n    if (tocDisplay) {\n      document.documentElement.setAttribute(\"data-toc-display\", tocDisplay);\n    }\n    const readingMode = localStorage.getItem('arxiv_html_paper_reading_mode');\n    if (readingMode) {\n      document.documentElement.setAttribute(\"data-reading-mode\", readingMode);\n    }\n    // Pre-apply spinout-banner dismissal here, before the banner paints, so it\n    // never flashes in only to be hidden later by the deferred arxiv-header.js.\n    // Key matches arxiv-header.js: \"arxiv-banner-dismissed:\" + data-banner-name.\n    if (localStorage.getItem('arxiv-banner-dismissed:spinout-nonprofit')) {\n      document.documentElement.setAttribute(\"data-banner-dismissed\", \"\");\n    }\n  }\n  // Run as soon as JS starts, to minimize repainting\n  initializeReadingPreferences();\n</script>\n<link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\" sizes=\"180x180\"\n  href=\"/static/browse/0.3.4/images/icons/apple-touch-icon.png\">\n<link rel=\"icon\" type=\"image/png\" sizes=\"32x32\"\n  href=\"/static/browse/0.3.4/images/icons/favicon-32x32.png\">\n<link rel=\"icon\" type=\"image/png\" sizes=\"16x16\"\n  href=\"/static/browse/0.3.4/images/icons/favicon-16x16.png\">\n<link rel=\"manifest\" href=\"/static/browse/0.3.4/images/icons/site.webmanifest\">\n<link rel=\"mask-icon\" href=\"/static/browse/0.3.4/images/icons/safari-pinned-tab.svg\" color=\"#5bbad5\">\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" media=\"screen\" href=\"https://use.typekit.net/utz6mli.css\"><link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" media=\"screen\"\n  href=\"/static/base/1.0.1/css/arxiv-header-footer.css?v=20260626\"><style>\n  /* Banner pre-dismissal (set above before paint -> no flash-then-hide) and\n     reading-mode chrome hiding. */\n  html[data-banner-dismissed] .ds-announcement { display: none; }\n  html[data-reading-mode=\"enabled\"] .ds-announcement,\n  html[data-reading-mode=\"enabled\"] .ds-site-footer { display: none; }\n  /* Keep the announcement text dark on the Open-Blue band in both colour themes\n     (otherwise it inherits the paper's warm-wash text in dark mode and washes out). */\n  .ds-announcement-text { color: var(--arxiv-ink, #1c1a17); }\n</style>\n<script defer src=\"/static/base/1.0.1/js/arxiv-header.js?v=20260626\"></script>\n</head>\n<body>\n<dialog id=\"modal-form\" aria-labelledby=\"modal-title\" closedby=\"any\">\n  <form id=\"modal-form-content\" method=\"dialog\" enctype=\"multipart/form-data\">\n    <header class=\"modal-header\">\n      <h5 id=\"modal-title\" class=\"modal-title\">Report GitHub Issue</h5>\n      <button type=\"submit\" formnovalidate class=\"modal-close\" aria-label=\"Close\">×</button>\n    </header>\n\n    <div class=\"modal-body\">\n      <label for=\"form_title\">Title:</label>\n      <input class=\"form-control\" id=\"form_title\" name=\"form_title\" required placeholder=\"Enter title\">\n\n      <p id=\"selectedTextModalDescription\" hidden>Content selection saved. Describe the issue below:</p>\n\n      <label for=\"description\">Description:</label>\n      <textarea class=\"form-control\" id=\"description\" name=\"description\" required maxlength=\"500\"\n        placeholder=\"500 characters maximum\"></textarea>\n    </div>\n\n    <footer class=\"modal-footer\">\n      <button type=\"submit\" value=\"internal-report\" class=\"sr-only modal-submit\">Submit without GitHub</button>\n      <button type=\"submit\" value=\"github-report\" class=\"modal-submit\">Submit in GitHub</button>\n    </footer>\n  </form>\n</dialog><div class=\"ds-announcement\" id=\"announcement-banner\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Announcement\"\n    data-banner-name=\"spinout-nonprofit\">\n    <img class=\"ds-announcement-glyph\" src=\"/static/base/1.0.1/images/icons/smileybones-small.svg\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n    <span class=\"ds-announcement-text\">arXiv is now an independent nonprofit!</span>\n    <a class=\"ds-announcement-link\" href=\"https://info.arxiv.org/about\">Learn more</a>\n    <button type=\"button\" class=\"ds-announcement-close\" aria-label=\"Dismiss announcement\">&times;</button>\n  </div>\n\n<header class=\"arxiv-html-header\">\n  <div class=\"html-header-logo\">\n    <a href=\"/\"><img alt=\"arXiv logo\" class=\"logo desktop-only\" width=\"100\"\n        src=\"/static/base/1.0.1/images/arxiv-logo-primary-light.svg\">\n      <span class=\"sr-only\">Back to arXiv</span>\n    </a>\n  </div>\n  <!--TOC, dark mode, links-->\n  <nav class=\"html-header-nav\">\n    <a class=\"header-button hover-effect desktop-only\" href=\"https://info.arxiv.org/about/accessible_HTML.html\"\n      target=\"_blank\">Why HTML?</a>\n    <a class=\"header-button\" title=\"Report an Issue\" href=\"#\" title=\"Report an issue\"\n      onclick=\"event.preventDefault(); showModalForm();\">\n      <svg role=\"presentation\" class=\"mobile-only toggle-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\" height=\"1.25rem\"\n        viewBox=\"0 0 640 640\">\n        <path